From: Talos Linux <bugs@siderolabs.com>
Subject: [PATCH] boot: do not pre-load the image into a source buffer

systemd v261 changed shim_load_image() to read the entire image (for Talos,
a ~100 MiB UKI) into a pool buffer via EFI_SIMPLE_FILE_SYSTEM_PROTOCOL and
pass it to BS->LoadImage() as SourceBuffer. Before, SourceBuffer was NULL and
the firmware read the file itself. Upstream commit 5580db885, motivated by
AMI firmware that misreads an ESP located on an optical drive.

This flips the firmware onto a different PE loading path, and the call is not
defensive: the return value of the read is discarded, and a short read
produces a truncated buffer whose declared size matches. EDK2's
PeCoffLoaderImageReadFromMemory() does not bound section copies against the
source size, so it will copy sections from past the end of the allocation.

Some firmware faults with a synchronous exception before the kernel is
entered, when booting the ISO as an El Torito CD/DVD:

    https://github.com/siderolabs/talos/issues/14029

Restore the systemd <= 260 behavior of letting the firmware load the image.

--- a/src/boot/shim.c
+++ b/src/boot/shim.c
@@ -93,21 +93,24 @@
         if (have_shim)
                 install_security_override(shim_validate, NULL);
 
-        _cleanup_free_ char *source_buffer = NULL;
-        size_t source_size = 0;
-
-        /* For some AMI firmware, BS->LoadImage() does not read correctly when the file comes the ESP on an
-         * optical drive. But the simple filesystem protocol does work. So we try to load it. If that does
-         * not work, we let BS->LoadImage() try instead.
-         */
-        (void) load_file_from_simple_filesystem(device_path, &source_buffer, &source_size);
-
+        /* Upstream reads the entire image into a pool buffer via the simple filesystem protocol here and
+         * hands it to BS->LoadImage() as SourceBuffer, to work around AMI firmware that does not read
+         * correctly from an ESP on an optical drive.
+         *
+         * That makes the firmware take a completely different code path in its PE loader, and it is not
+         * robust: the read result is ignored, and a short read yields a truncated image which the firmware
+         * will happily load sections out of, past the end of the buffer. Some firmware faults with a
+         * synchronous exception before the kernel is ever entered:
+         *
+         *     https://github.com/siderolabs/talos/issues/14029
+         *
+         * Let the firmware load the image itself, as systemd <= 260 did. */
         EFI_STATUS ret = BS->LoadImage(
                         /* BootPolicy= */ boot_policy,
                         parent,
                         (EFI_DEVICE_PATH *) device_path,
-                        source_buffer,
-                        source_size,
+                        /* SourceBuffer= */ NULL,
+                        /* SourceSize= */ 0,
                         ret_image);
         if (have_shim)
                 uninstall_security_override();
